00:06:49.514 --> 00:06:53.028
Speaker 1: It is the ultimate trap of the graphical user interface. You see a Gantt chart

112
00:06:53.028 --> 00:06:56.542
Speaker 1: in the old software, and then you see a Gantt chart in the new software,

113
00:06:56.542 --> 00:06:58.885
Speaker 1: and you just assume the engine underneath them is identical.

114
00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:00.759
Speaker 2: And it couldn't be further from the truth.

115
00:07:00.759 --> 00:07:07.006
Speaker 1: But the source documentation makes a really harsh distinction here. Microsoft is actively divorcing collaborative

116
00:07:07.006 --> 00:07:12.004
Speaker 1: project execution from what they call mature project portfolio management, or PPM.

117
00:07:12.004 --> 00:07:17.359
Speaker 2: This is a huge philosophical shift. Historically, organizations used Project Online to do both of

118
00:07:17.359 --> 00:07:19.501
Speaker 2: those things at the same time.

119
00:07:19.501 --> 00:07:20.438
Speaker 1: Right, all in one bucket.

120
00:07:20.438 --> 00:07:26.061
Speaker 2: Right. They used it to manage the daily, collaborative tasks of their teams, who's doing

121
00:07:26.061 --> 00:07:31.683
Speaker 2: what on Tuesday, but they also used it to manage the complex, multi-year financial portfolios

122
00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:33.557
